    "field": "Climate change impacts",
    "problem": "It remains unclear how escalating climate extremes translate into unprecedented cumulative exposure over a person's lifetime, making it difficult to quantify the number of people who will face such life-long conditions under different warming scenarios.",
    "method": "The proposed method combines climate and impact models with demographic data to project the fraction of birth cohorts facing unprecedented lifetime exposure to six climate extremes, defined as exposure exceeding the 99.99th percentile of that expected in a pre-industrial climate.",
    "task": "The task is to project the number of people from different birth cohorts who will experience an unprecedented cumulative lifetime exposure to six climate extremes by combining climate models, impact models, and demographic data under various global warming pathways.",
